m4_changequote()
kathara-connect(1) -- Connect to a Kathara device
=============================================

## SYNOPSIS

`kathara connect` [`-h`] [`-d` <DIRECTORY> \| `-v` \| `--lab-name` <LAB_NAME>]  
[`--shell` <SHELL>] [`-l`]  
<DEVICE_NAME>

## DESCRIPTION

Open a shell in device DEVICE_NAME.

## OPTIONS

* `-h`, `--help`:
    Show a help message and exit.

* `-d` <DIRECTORY>, `--directory` <DIRECTORY>:
    Specify the folder containing the network scenario.

    Connect to a Kathara device belonging to a network scenario that is located inside DIRECTORY.  
	If no `-d` option is provided, assume the network scenario is located in the current directory.
	This option cannot be used in conjunction with `-v`, `--vmachine` or `--lab-name`.

* `-v`, `--vmachine`:
	The device has been started with vstart command.

	This option cannot be used in conjunction with `-d`, `--directory` or `--lab-name`.

* `--lab-name` <LAB_NAME>:
    Specify the name of the network scenario containing the specified device.

    Only works for a network scenario started with a name, i.e., one that declares `LAB_NAME` in `kathara-lab.conf`(5) or that was started through the Kathara Python APIs.
    Otherwise, the network scenario is identified by its path, and must be selected with `-d` or `--directory`.

    Settings in the `kathara.conf`(5) file of the network scenario directory are not loaded. If it changes `manager_type` or `remote_url`, the network scenario cannot be found by name.

    This option cannot be used in conjunction with `-d`, `--directory`, `-v` or `--vmachine`.

* `--command` <SHELL>:
    Command that should be executed inside the device.

    By default, the shell specified in `kathara.conf`(5) file is executed. This option overrides this setting.

* `-l`, `--logs`:
    Print device startup logs before launching the shell.

    By default it does not print the startup logs, this behaviour is not customizable by the user.

* `<DEVICE_NAME>:
    Name of the device to connect to.


## EXAMPLES

	kathara connect -v pc1

Connects to a device called `pc1`, started with `kathara-vstart`(1).

	kathara connect as1r1

Connects to a device called `as1r1` belonging to a network scenario located in current folder and started with `kathara-lstart`(1).

	kathara connect --lab-name mylab pc1

Connects to a device called `pc1` belonging to a network scenario named `mylab`, created by name through the Kathara API.

